=== Prompt ===
Who is Nelson Mandela?

=== Response ===
Nelson Mandela was a South African anti-apartheid revolutionary, politician, and philanthropist who served as President of South Africa from 1994 to 1999. He was the country's first black head of state and the first elected in a fully representative democratic election. His government focused on dismantling the legacy of apartheid by tackling institutionalized racism and fostering racial reconciliation.

Mandela was born on July 18, 1918, in Mvezo, Eastern Cape, South Africa. He studied law at the University of Fort Hare and the University of the Witwatersrand, where he became involved in anti-colonial and African nationalist politics. He co-founded the Youth League of the African National Congress (ANC) in 1944 and was elected its president in 1991.

For 27 years, Mandela was imprisoned for his political activism against apartheid, a system of institutionalized racial segregation and discrimination that governed South Africa from 1948 until 1994. He was released in 1990 and worked with President F.W. de Klerk to negotiate an end to apartheid, leading to the establishment of multiracial elections in 1994, in which he was elected president.

Mandela received numerous awards for his work, including the Nobel Peace Prize in 1993. He retired from public life in 2004, but continued to be an advocate for human rights and social justice until his death on December 5, 2013.

His legacy includes the creation of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission, aimed at addressing the crimes committed during apartheid, and his emphasis on reconciliation and forgiveness, which helped to stabilize South Africa after the end of apartheid.

